title: News from Brest-Litovsk
new-page: true
view-if: german_negotiations = 6
max-visits: 1
tags: event
on-arrival: {!
  Q.morale *= 0.8; Q.discipline *= 0.6; Q.war_weariness += 10; 
  Q.instability += 3; Q.train_capacity *= 0.95;
  Q.soldiers_unrest += 10; Q.peasants_unrest += 5; 
  Q.german_negotiations = 7; 
!}

= News from Brest-Litovsk

The Germans have finally replied to us with their peace terms:<br><ul>
    <li>Cession of Finland, the Baltic states, Belarus, Ukraine, Poland and Kars and Batum, and cessation of war between Russia and any territories therein.</li>
    <li>Immediate demobilization of the Russian Army (both the old army and the new) and the Red Guards, and internment or dismantling of the Russian navy.</li>
    <li>Favorable trade with Germany and protection of German business and capitalists in Russia, along with payment of a significant indemnity.</li>
    <li>Cessation of revolutionary propaganda within the Central Powers.</li>
</ul>
  
The Germans have informed us that we must accept the terms as is within 48 hours (much of which has already elapsed). 

Lenin is absolutely adamant on the need for peace, and is even threatening to resign from the Central Committee and Sovnarkom if the terms are not accepted. 

- @accept
- @reject


@reject
title: If Lenin resigns, so be it! 
choose-if: leftcom_strength >= ((leninist_strength + moderate_strength) * 3)
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--leftcom); font-weight: bold;">Leftcoms</span> aren't to risk this. 

@accept
title: The terms must be accepted. 
on-arrival: {!
  Q.leftcom_strength -= 5;
  Q.leninist_dissent -= 5; Q.leftcom_dissent += 10;
  Q.b_dissent += 0.15;
!}

The terms are narrowly approved by a vote of 7 in favor, 4 against, and 4 abstentions. 

The four no-votes (Bukharin, Lomov, Uritsky, and Bubnov), along with several other prominent Bolshevik leaders, have decided to tender resignations of their own, so that they may be free to campaign against the treaty both within and outside the party. Although, we may be able to delay their resignations by signalling that agitation against the peace will be allowed.  

- @disallow
- @allow

@disallow
title: Enforce party unity, even if it means a split! 
